# Wacki Arch Package

This PKGBUILD intentionally does not download or redistribute original
Wacki: Kosmiczna rozgrywka game files. Upstream ships GPL engine code only.

Before running `makepkg`, create a local source archive named
`wacki-data.tar.gz` next to this PKGBUILD. The archive must contain:

- `WACKI.EXE`
- `dane_*.dta`

Recommended command:

```sh
mkdir -p wacki-data
cp /path/to/original-disc/WACKI.EXE wacki-data/
cp /path/to/original-disc/dane_*.dta wacki-data/
bsdtar -czf wacki-data.tar.gz -C wacki-data .
makepkg -si
```

The fixed archive name is deliberate: makepkg source files must be URLs or
files available in the PKGBUILD directory, and one local archive avoids fragile
`dane_*.dta` glob handling in package metadata.

The built package embeds the required sections from `WACKI.EXE` into the engine
binary and installs the data files as canonical `Dane_NN.dta` names under
`/usr/share/wacki/data`. This works around upstream v1.0.4 not probing fully
lowercase `dane_*.dta` on case-sensitive filesystems. Do not redistribute the
built package unless your original game license permits that.

The `/usr/bin/wacki` launcher stores `Wacki.sav`, `wacki.cfg`, logs, and
screenshots under `${XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}/wacki`. It sets
`WACKI_PATH=/usr/share/wacki/data` unless you already provided `WACKI_PATH`.
Set `WACKI_USER_DIR` to use a different writable directory.
